WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.980
The southern region of the universe is shining blue.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.970
That is the light of the Second Wave...

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.450
The fate of the human race rests upon the Great Mission...

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.840
The great plan that has spanned over 189 years is about to begin.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:28.510
It is December 19, 2356.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.890
Episode Ten:
Welcome Back

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.760
There is a message from Commander Del Toro of the Odyssey.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:04.900
From Miguel?

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.150
Orihara, how are things over there?

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.790
When this is over, come over and visit.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.530
Let's work on the arrangements for next year's athletic festival.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.550
Well, next year, we're finally going to win, got it?

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.980
One minute until the Second Wave makes contact!

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.120
Beginning countdown.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.280
57, 56, 55, 54...

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.080
Right now, the moment when the contact will occur has come near.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:41.900
30 seconds to go...

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:47.390
28, 27, 26, 25, 24...

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.310
Ten seconds to go...

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.550
Eight, seven, six...

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:00.850
It's here!

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.930
The Second Wave has made contact!

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.060
It's beautiful...

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.210
All systems operating normally!

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.680
Impact absorption rate 100%!

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.220
The plan... was successful!

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.600
Thank goodness, right, Shima-chan?

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:41.470
Yeah.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.730
Congratulations.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:44.760
Congratulations.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.710
With this, all we have left is to wait for it to pass through.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.970
W-What the...?

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:53.900
What?

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.040
What in the world is going on?

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.130
Report our current status!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.210
Is the Great Wall all right?

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.480
It is currently operating at 105%!

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.080
However, a great number of objects have penetrated it!

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.580
To all Ora-avis Machine formations!

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.750
From here on, we will be proceeding with interception actions!

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:22.730
Roger!

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.200
It's time to show them the results of our hard work.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.080
Protect the generators!

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.270
Roger!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.260
Didn't they say that, according to the calculations...

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.120
...the Great Wall wouldn't get penetrated?

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.860
"Truth is stranger than fiction."

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.420
Is this a little off?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:21.950
It's completely off.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.280
But isn't this a chance to show off our skills?

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:27.300
That's true.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.490
Go!

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.840
Oh, they've dispersed!

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.310
So what is this?

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.440
The state of the mission.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.950
You're accessing the main server again?

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.890
This time you'll be expelled.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.080
Quite a few have gotten through.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.090
But when they hit the barrier, they decelerate quite a bit...

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.560
...and they're all small.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.460
It looks like right now, the Ora-avis battalion is dealing with it completely.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.790
So what about Shipon and the others?

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.070
Katase, here comes one!

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.140
Katase, don't just sit there.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:11.700
Put up the barrier!

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:12.700
Otherwise, you'll get hurt!

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.630
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.650
Just like that, Shima-chan.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.620
Otoyama...

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:29.990
It's amazing.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:34.100
This is 0304, my propulsion unit has been taken out!

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.360
I've lost control! I've lost control!

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.060
A meteorite is coming in on a collision course!

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:40.840
Look out!

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.250
I cannot dodge! I cannot dodge!

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:42.800
Shima-chan!

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.020
Oh, no, Katase!

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.560
Katase's unit has been damaged!?

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.360
Hey, let me see it.
is Shipon all right?

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.090
W-Wait a second, calm down... 
I can't see!

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.040
Oww!
See? She's all right.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.470
It just scraped her unit.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:16.120
It says that Kouta is escorting her back.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:18.570
Oh, man...

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.080
That was scary...

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:22.510
I'm going to go meet Shipon!

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:23.780
M-Me too!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:24.960
Rinna!

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.370
The station's internal systems have restarted.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:33.960
What's the damage situation?

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:37.860
The Great Wall is taking the shockwave itself...

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.350
...so the damage is due only to small meteorites.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.640
We are currently confirming the effect on the Earth itself.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.410
However, presently one generator at L4...

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.980
...and two at L5 have been struck by meteorites...

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.060
...and there have been several people injured.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:51.420
How is the Moon?

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.170
Several meteorites have fallen on the surface of the Moon...

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:55.650
...but there is no damage to the underground city.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:00.360
Assign about half of the Ora-avis machines to the Moon's perimeter.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:01.140
Roger.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.460
It looks like we'll get through this somehow, doesn't it?

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.930
At this rate, as long as nothing else happens.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:24.210
Whoa.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.050
Katase!
Miss Katase!

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.280
Mr. Shirogane...

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.590
Katase, are you all right?

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.370
Are you hurt?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.940
I'm all right...

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:40.060
Shipon! Kouta!

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.460
Everyone.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.580
Hey, you guys, what are you doing in a place like this?

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.260
Shipon!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.290
Thank goodness!

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.060
Geez...
Shipon!

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.170
What the, you're in the best of health!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.160
I was worried, Shima Katase!

00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:58.940
Why, you!

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:01.740
Arisa!

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:02.820
Huh?

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.210
Shipon!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:11.960
I... I... I thought that I would do my best...

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.620
...but I wasn't able to do anything well...

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:19.470
...and I came back without doing anything...

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:30.950
Shipon...

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:35.930
What are you talking about?

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:40.030
You saved a fellow pilot and came back unhurt.

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:41.740
You did well, Katase.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.940
Be proud of yourself, proud!

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.160
Mr. Shirogane...

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.330
Oh, you do say good things once in a while.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:52.010
I always say good things. Listen properly.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.200
Yes, yes. 
What?

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.390
C-Commander!

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.490
W-What was that just now?

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.600
What's happened...?

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:49.900
This is...

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:53.800
The giant meteor is approximately 100 kilometers in diameter!

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.090
It's currently on a course to collide with the Earth!

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.860
Order all units within possible distance to attack!

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.170
This feels kind of useless...

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.990
It's too big. Beams like these won't be able to do anything to it.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.440
So it's going to keep heading straight for the Earth.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:31.280
Is there nothing we can do?

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:34.310
The firepower of the Ora-avis Machines can't put a dent in it!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.160
It is impossible to destroy the target!

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.570
Three generators at L4 and two generators at L5...

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.960
...have already been struck by meteorites!

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.450
The Great Wall's output is declining!

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:46.370
Commander! The hole in the barrier is so big...

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.920
...that the Great Wall's balance is going to deteriorate!

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:51.750
At this rate, at this rate...

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.480
...the entire Great Wall is going to collapse!

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:57.070
Commander...

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.850
There's got to be...

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:02.330
There still has to be something that we can do...

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:06.350
Damn it, the meteor and the hole are both too big.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:07.680
The Ora-avis Machines can't do anything about them...

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.240
"Can't do anything about them"...?

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.360
Then what's going to happen?

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:13.610
The Earth will be destroyed by the meteor.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.400
If the barrier is destroyed...

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.870
...then the Moon, the colonies, and us, it's all over...

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:20.950
It can't be...

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:24.650
Then we're going to die?

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.110
If we use that...

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:37.500
What?

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.790
If we use that, then we might be able to do something.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:42.210
Use that?

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.450
Is it possible?

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.800
Well, certainly, with its power.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.290
But we'll have to prepare it in order for it to move.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.980
Commander, there's an emergency message from the campus.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:55.480
From the campus?

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:00.120
It's heavy...

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.680
This time we have to undo all of them?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.270
It was all for nothing.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:05.890
What did you say?

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.410
The giant thing we got from the Earth!

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:11.300
In order for it to operate its gigantic humanoid form...

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:14.480
...the entire thing is equipped with gravity wave generators.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.010
If we open all of them...

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:18.560
...we might be able to close up the hole that opened up in the barrier.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:25.700
Shirogane, we were just thinking the same thing.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:29.170
But the problem is the time and people needed to prepare it.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.800
And we haven't tested its control system, have we?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.660
The controls were made into a two-seater and the functions divided.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:40.330
In ten minutes, it will become, at the very least, functional.

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:43.510
Mr. Hutter... but what about pilots?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.280
We will pilot it.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:46.200
You are?

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:48.530
I'm Kouta Otoyama, a preparatory student, and...

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:49.870
I'm Shima Katase.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:52.270
But you're both still preparatory students, right?

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.620
All of the pilots are currently out.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.960
And even if we called some back, they wouldn't make it in time.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.690
Are you saying we leave the fate of the Earth in the hands of these children?

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.850
Commander!

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:03.520
This is all we have.

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:07.280
Even if the possibility is small, let's try and stake our lives on it!

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.600
Please believe in the students!

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.070
We don't have the time to hesitate.

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.960
It doesn't matter who, but get the controls over there started up!

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.160
Prepare the Infinity for launch!

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.240
All right, we've got permission!

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:28.040
Hurry with that work, we don't have any time!

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:36.490
That is a beam cannon made specifically for Infi.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.850
Whoa, it's huge...

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:42.210
It's in the third container, so go and pick it up with the Infinity.

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:45.020
Destroy that giant meteor with it.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:47.050
This is the manual.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:49.880
All right, this is the last one.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:54.530
All right, lift it up!
Mr. Shirogane, we finished them all!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:58.350
Commander, we've finished detaching all the wires.

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.370
Thank you, Shirogane.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.800
Get everyone out of there immediately.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:03.580
Roger!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:05.740
Each section, final check!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:10.290
What's that?

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:11.770
A charm.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:13.440
Hmm?

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.290
All right, shall we go?

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.220
From this point, the interior of the S Room will become a vacuum.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.280
The Infinity is moving to the seventh hatch.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.700
The third elevator's gate is open.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:29.260
The Infinity is on the hatch, all gates are closing.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.470
All systems are go!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.640
The Infinity is being lifted up!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.110
Launch preparations are okay.

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.030
Entering countdown.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.120
Ten seconds to go.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:06.010
Eight. Seven. Six.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:09.800
Five. Four. Three. Two.

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:10.760
One!

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:13.010
Infinity, launch!

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:29.320
Is this the world that Otoyama sees?

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.330
An order to retreat?

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:35.630
What's going on?

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:40.310
Wh-What the...!?

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:41.610
That's...

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:49.910
The blaster has been connected to Infi.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:51.620
The target is locked on.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.510
The energy loading is...

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:56.690
...this one!

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:57.600
It's okay!

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.270
There aren't any obstacles between us and the target.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:02.860
Here we go, Shima-chan!

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:03.760
All right!

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:06.310
Fire!

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:31.670
Incredible...

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:35.630
Explosion confirmed! The meteor has successfully been destroyed!

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:36.890
All right!!

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:37.970
We did it!

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:39.160
Shima-chan.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:39.820
Yeah!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.830
Please take care of the fragments!

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:46.600
What?

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.800
Miss... Katase?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.680
Release all of the generators.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:55.980
Releasing.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:06.310
Prepare to open the field.

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.010
Preparing to open the field.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.400
Form the field.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:15.790
Forming the field.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.240
Here we go, Shima-chan!

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:21.000
Okay!

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.490
The Infinity has completed extending its barrier.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:47.830
All that's left is to see how long it will hold up.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:51.010
Let's believe in the luck of those children.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.500
The temperature inside the unit is rising.

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:56.020
It just passed 35 degrees Celsius.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.260
How are the generators?

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.660
They're all operating normally...

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:02.290
...but several of them have passed their load limits.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:04.340
All that's left is to see who has more patience.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:30.950
Wh-What?

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:32.910
The light... has disappeared?

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.040
The flow is stopping...

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.010
We have confirmation!

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:48.350
The Second Wave has completely passed through!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.210
The Great Mission has succeeded!

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.800
All right!

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.840
It's over. It's over, Shima-chan!

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.290
You did well, Katase.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.440
Commander, there are recovered transmissions...

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.500
...from both the Mars and Venus areas.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:12.300
It appears that both are all right.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.030
There is also a transmission from the Ultima.

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.950
It appears that all hands are all right there, too!

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.500
All right, Rinna!

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.500
Isn't that wonderful, Rinna?

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:34.330
That girl... saved the world...

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.360
I'm amazed.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.440
This year's new students really are unbelievable.

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:41.730
You're wrong. We all saved the world.

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:46.740
"We few, we happy few, we band of brothers."

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.880
From Charley V?

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:50.550
It's Henry.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:57.060
Whoa, what's that?

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:02.090
It might be hard to believe, but isn't that an aurora?

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.470
What, really?

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:06.520
Wow! This is the first time I've seen one!

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.830
I don't know if it'll connect or not...

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:10.770
...but let's try calling Shima.

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:15.310
Oh, sure thing. Calling, calling my big sister.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:18.410
Um, I wonder if it'll connect.

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:21.610
There's no need to worry.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:35.020
Sol System Local Time: Year 2356 - December 19 - 14:13

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:34.760
The Second Wave has passed through the Sol System

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:40.650
Humanity has survived

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:44.950
Uh... What the?

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:48.940
Oh, it's a phone transmission. My cell phone, where's my cell phone?

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.630
It's amazing that you can have that set up at a time like this...

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:54.370
Yes, hello?

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
And still I looked up

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:06.520
It's Shima!

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:07.300
It's Arisa!

00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:08.890
The Great Mission has ended without any problems...

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:10.630
...so the preparatory students' classes have gone to the next level!

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:13.600
And the Biancas are switched over to the DLS system!

00:23:13.670 --> 00:23:15.470
DLS - the Direct Link System.

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:19.170
The information flows directly into your head, kind of like a groove.

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:20.970
In any case, it looks kind of bad for your health.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:24.410
What? R-Really? I wonder if your head starts to hurt...

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:26.310
Or it might be something worse...

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:27.370
What!?

00:23:27.450 --> 00:23:29.770
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe, "The Real You."

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:30.550
Please look forward to it!

